; lane D — the drive loop: the two instances of the generated engine, the program
; conversion and the ordinal pin, the differential between them, and the first numbers.
;   test_engine  G0 (p42 / pFork / pAwait) on Fast AND Ref; the 37 byte goldens of
;                ocaml/eff/goldens run at fuel 1000 on both, with outcome, exits, the
;                fiber-table projection, the trace rows and the store row compared row by
;                row (differential D1 in miniature); the M17 ordinal pin against
;                ocaml/eff/eff_manifest.txt with a transposition mutation test;
;                `replay_steps` at |tape|+1; a count of the two `failwith` rows of the
;                generated prelude; and the W1/W2 bench cells (a measurement, printed, not
;                a gate).  It reads ocaml/eff/goldens and ocaml/eff/eff_manifest.txt by an
;                ancestor walk from the cwd — $E4_EFF_GOLDENS and $E4_EFF_MANIFEST override.

(test
 (name test_engine)
 (modules test_engine)
 (libraries effect4_engine effect4_eff unix))

; lane X — the differential over every corpus, three engines.
;   test_diff   `Corpora` (the 37 byte goldens, the truth corpus's Lean-cut wire goldens,
;               and 500 generated well-typed Eff programs) x `E4_diff` (thirteen
;               projections per position) x three engines: `Api_gen` as generated (the
;               oracle, built here into an `E4_engine.INSTANCE`), `Ref` (the seam over
;               list twins — the extern-row half) and `Fast` (the substituted carriers —
;               the carrier half).  Every position of every replay is compared on both
;               pairs; the tapes are drawn from the machine as it runs, so they are
;               admissible by construction.  It also discharges lane C's OWED FB1, records
;               why DF-2/DF-3 are not run, and reports the engines against
;               harness/truth/corpus.json.  Paths are found by an ancestor walk from the
;               cwd — $E4_EFF_GOLDENS, $E4_HEX_GOLDENS and $E4_TRUTH_CORPUS override.
;               `effect4_gen` is named here and NOWHERE in the library: the third engine
;               is a test-only functor application.

(test
 (name test_diff)
 (modules test_diff)
 (libraries effect4_engine effect4_eff effect4_gen))

; lane Q3 — query: the persistent log, its incremental indexes, and the query API.
;   test_log     E4_log L1-L5, the public-log codec (E4_logindex.parse_run_event_row) over
;                the rows E4_engine renders, and E4_logindex X1-X3 with the segment law.
;                Pure: no engine, no machine, no tape.
;   test_query   E4_query Q1/Q3/Q4, `cost` exact against a counted replay, the
;                INV-TAPE-1(query) repo gate (it greps e4_query.mli for a signature whose
;                RESULT type mentions `source` or `tape`), and DF-3 (query agreement): for
;                the 37 byte goldens of ocaml/eff/goldens, `E4_query.at s i` equals the
;                machine the tape prefix replays, on all thirteen E4_diff projections, at
;                EVERY i for the ten longest tapes and sampled for the rest — plus the
;                mutation test (an `at` built from a different tape prefix must go red).
;                It reads ocaml/eff/goldens by an ancestor walk — $E4_EFF_GOLDENS overrides.
;   bench_query  the B-Q3a-c and B-Q5a-c cells with the acceptance verdict per cell.  An
;                executable, not a test: a bench is a measurement, not a gate.

(test
 (name test_log)
 (modules test_log)
 (libraries effect4_engine))

(test
 (name test_query)
 (modules test_query)
 (libraries effect4_engine effect4_eff))

