; lane B — the bench matrix: one receipt with every number the effort claimed, re-measured
; on the landed engine (docs/research/2026-09-08-engine-bench.md).
;   e4_engine_bench  W1 (the nine truth programs + the 37 byte goldens), W2 (chain of
;                    refMake at n = 100/300/1000/2000/8000), W3 (the 500 generated
;                    programs), W4 (fan-out N x M yields) over the THREE engines
;                    (`Api_gen` untouched, `Ref`, `Fast`), plus the domain sweep of 200 and
;                    2 000 `pTwo` machines over 1/2/4/8 domains through `E4_sched` with the
;                    real `Fast` engine, and the AC1-AC9 acceptance table.  An executable,
;                    not a test: a bench is a measurement, not a gate.  Driven by
;                    ../tools/run-bench.sh, which runs every bench binary of the engine and
;                    cas test directories into one Markdown receipt.

(executable
 (name e4_engine_bench)
 (modules e4_engine_bench)
 (libraries effect4_engine effect4_eff effect4_gen unix))

; lane G3 — the fiber table's maintained completed view (docs/research/
; 2026-09-08-engine-lane-g3-delivery.md).
;   prop_fibers_view  E4_fibers_view FV1-FV8 against the LIST twin (which walks Lean's
;                     filterMap at read time) and against E4_table.filter_map over the
;                     carrier's own table, with the FIBERS module type of the generated
;                     functor ascribed to both carriers.  FV8 is the sharing law: a write
;                     that does not change an exit leaves the answer PHYSICALLY the same
;                     list, which is why `completedExits` costs nothing per step.
(test
 (name prop_fibers_view)
 (modules prop_fibers_view)
 (libraries effect4_engine))
